Auxiliary power, cooling, controls and hidden dependencies (@pe-auxiliaries: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electrical-power-engineering, #source "../sources/Hydroelectric-Mechanical-and-Electrical-Design-USACE.lingua#r_1N0D32HTSXMVJ1VRW9TNTYV9P8", #source "../sources/Conduct-of-Power-Operations-and-Maintenance-FIST.lingua#r_4JS2N9S01A3KTMH37TXMVSPPYC", #source "../sources/Excitation-Systems-Hydroelectric-FIST-2026.lingua#r_725R40RX14YMRTQNWKGHY12JCN", #electrical-power-engineering "Condition-monitoring-diagnostics-and-failure-hypotheses.lingua#r_6P53MN2MTNTE5PQ585XX6YFD0E") { r_07SBEGZTPXB61KPF875G4WMH53
**Read:** [Mechanical and Electrical Design of Hydroelectric Power Plants — USACE](../sources/Hydroelectric-Mechanical-and-Electrical-Design-USACE.lingua#r_1N0D32HTSXMVJ1VRW9TNTYV9P8), whole applicable auxiliary and control/service chapters; [Conduct of power operations and maintenance — FIST](../sources/Conduct-of-Power-Operations-and-Maintenance-FIST.lingua#r_4JS2N9S01A3KTMH37TXMVSPPYC), both complete operational/maintenance contexts; [Excitation Systems for Hydroelectric Units — FIST 3-14](../sources/Excitation-Systems-Hydroelectric-FIST-2026.lingua#r_725R40RX14YMRTQNWKGHY12JCN), complete relevant excitation/auxiliary treatment.

An electrical plant depends on small systems that can be critical to its large output: DC batteries/chargers, trip supplies, lubrication, cooling, excitation, compressed air where used, controls, instrumentation and communication. Their rated power can be modest while their loss prevents starting, protection or continued service.

Draw dependency paths separately from the main energy path. Compare normal, startup, fault, isolated and restoration states, including what powers the systems needed to start the main source. A standby resource that needs an unavailable shared fuel/cooling/control supply is not independent redundancy.

Read the complete relevant [Mechanical and Electrical Design of Hydroelectric Power Plants — USACE](../sources/Hydroelectric-Mechanical-and-Electrical-Design-USACE.lingua#r_1N0D32HTSXMVJ1VRW9TNTYV9P8) facility chapters and [Conduct of power operations and maintenance — FIST](../sources/Conduct-of-Power-Operations-and-Maintenance-FIST.lingua#r_4JS2N9S01A3KTMH37TXMVSPPYC) procedures. Build a small state/dependency account and test a common-cause interruption, maintenance outage and changed auxiliary condition. Connect electrical consequences to mechanical, thermal and material services through ordinary [Engineering — systems, design, construction, and operation](../../Engineering.lingua#r_5DA6VY09MAD2N8D9SH0FFJVV68) and [Ergon](../../../../ergon/Ergon.lingua#r_00000000000000000000002001) references. Report which physical evidence supports autonomy, duration and return to service. A single-line diagram and total generating capacity do not establish these continuing dependencies.

**Continue:** [Condition monitoring, diagnostics and failure hypotheses](Condition-monitoring-diagnostics-and-failure-hypotheses.lingua#r_6P53MN2MTNTE5PQ585XX6YFD0E).

**Return:** [Electrical power engineering — sources, networks, machines and continuing service](../Electrical-power-engineering.lingua#r_300EPNGATK7PHWNZCQFBXGZFCQ).
